    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "replacing the cable and the Sfp didn't change anything. still seeing the same spikes. it's almost like something is randomly messing with the signal just for a second and then leaving. i've seen people call these kinds of random glitches \"gremlins\" in the past, but that's just a joke. \n\nis there any actual technical reason why a signal would just sporadically drop or spike like this without leaving a clear error footprint in the logs?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "These random, transient signal degradations often point towards electromagnetic interference (EMI) affecting the hardware. EMI can cause momentary data corruption, which results in retransmissions and perceived jitter without triggering hard interface error counters. Another possibility, though less common, is faulty transceiver components within the device itself, which can fail sporadically under load.",
      "source": "target",
